# Go backend — sandbox

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), root [fail-fast-no-fallbacks.mdc](../../../../.cursor/rules/fail-fast-no-fallbacks.mdc),
[architecture-standard.mdc](../../../../.cursor/rules/architecture-standard.mdc), and [go-backend.mdc](../../../../.cursor/rules/go-backend.mdc).

## Layers

```
internal/app/api/sandbox/     transport (1 RPC = 1 file)
internal/sandbox/service/     thin orchestrator → usecase handlers
internal/sandbox/usecase/     command|query/<op> + support helpers
internal/sandbox/repository/  Store port + Postgres
internal/adapter/runner/
```

- JWT validator always wired. User sessions omit `room_id`; editor tokens are
  validated against the request's exact `editor:{room_id}` scope.
- `service.New()` / usecase `New` return an error on missing required deps — no mid-path invent defaults.
- Persistence: `repository.Store` (mockery), not concrete `*Repository` in service/usecase.
- Running rows require a unique claim token + lease; only token-matched terminal
  updates may clear a claim. Runner process output always uses bounded draining writers.
